# Lessons Learned
By completing this lab, I gained practical experience in writing Bash shell scripts to automate basic tasks in Linux. I learned how to accept and process user input using the read command and how to use conditional statements such as if, elif, and else to make decisions based on user input.

I also developed a better understanding of numeric comparisons and program flow control in shell scripting. Through the username validation exercise, I learned how to enforce input requirements by checking character types and string length. Additionally, I gained experience using regular expressions to validate user input and ensure that it met specified criteria. Testing the scripts with different inputs helped me strengthen my troubleshooting and debugging skills.
